  "system_note": "Claim [[CLAIM-0004]] / Patient [[MRN-0044]] — Billed line 1: CPT 17110 (Destruction of benign lesion[s]), no modifier. Governing-policy lookup returned no is_target policy specifically restricting or redefining CPT 17110; a separate APC concept about modifier -25 was returned but is not a code-specific denial of 17110. The medical record documents the planned procedure (Pre-Operative Assessment), the intraoperative confirmation of the procedure, and a detailed operative note describing the single 0.8 cm seborrheic keratosis that was destroyed by curettage and electrodesiccation, with no specimen submitted (i.e., lesion destroyed in situ). These facts meet the clinical documentation expectations for a minor destruction procedure billed as 17110. Key supporting documentation: Pre-Operative Assessment & Anesthesia Evaluation (planned procedure = CPT 17110) (Pre-Operative Assessment & Anesthesia Evaluation, p. 16-17); Operative Note (procedure performed, lesion size/site, technique: curettage + electrodesiccation) (Operative Note, p. 25-26); Intraoperative Record confirming the correct procedure and that the lesion was destroyed in place (Intraoperative Record, p. 22-24). Therefore the record supports the billed CPT 17110 as submitted. Note: the claim also contains a same-day 99213-25 E/M line; the returned APC concept text about modifier -25 sets requirements for billing a separate E/M on the same day as a minor procedure. That E/M line should be reviewed against that policy separately, but it does not alter the determination for line 1 (17110).",
